Found and fixed the problem — it wasn't your credentials.

## Why you couldn't log in

Your site is being served by the **static preview server on port 8080** (`py -m http.server`), not XAMPP — port 80 has no server running right now. A static server cannot execute PHP, so the login POST returns **501**, and the app correctly falls back to its browser-side database. That fallback only contained the demo customer, so `admin@store.com` didn't exist there and sign-in was rejected with "Invalid email or password".

The console proves it exactly: `API 501 → API login failed, using fallback authentication`.

## The fix

Added `ensureSeedAdmins()` to [app.js](js/app.js) — it mirrors the two administrators from [noframe.sql](database/noframe.sql) into the offline fallback database on start-up, the same way the demo customer has always worked. Assets bumped to `?v=20261028`.

## Verified from a completely clean browser

I wiped every `noframe-*` key in storage, reloaded (fresh-visitor state), and signed in:

- **`admin@store.com` / `Admin@123`** → toast "Welcome back, Admin ✓", lands on `#/profile`, footer **Admin Portal →** link appears, `#/admin` opens the dashboard (Overview, Products, Categories, Orders, **Customers** tabs, stats showing 174 products).
- **`admin@noframe.com` / `admin123`** → also signs in and opens the dashboard.
- Customers tab lists all three accounts with their roles.

Console: no new errors — only the pre-existing PHP-API warnings plus the expected 501/404s from the static server.

## If you want the real MySQL-backed login

Start XAMPP (Apache + MySQL) so the site is served on port 80, and make sure the admin row is in the database — run the INSERT I gave you earlier against your existing `noframe` DB (don't re-import the whole file; it drops tables first). Then the PHP login path with bcrypt verification handles it. Until MySQL has the row, the browser fallback above is what lets you in, and admin-only writes still require a genuine admin session on the server — a faked local role can't pass `?action=save`'s 403.
