## Why you couldn't log in

Your site is being served by the **static preview server on port 8080** (`py -m http.server`), not XAMPP — I checked and nothing is listening on port 80 right now. A static server can't execute PHP, so the login POST returns **501**, and the app falls back to its browser-side database. That fallback contained only the demo customer, so `admin@store.com` didn't exist there and sign-in was rejected.

The console showed it precisely: `API 501 → API login failed, using fallback authentication`.

## The fix

I added `ensureSeedAdmins()` to [app.js](js/app.js), which mirrors both administrators from [noframe.sql](database/noframe.sql) into the offline fallback database on start-up — the same courtesy the demo customer always had. Assets bumped to `?v=20261028`.

