**NoFrame Admin (`admin@noframe.com` / `admin123`) now has full dashboard access, and the product form covers everything you listed — main categories, sub-categories, colours and sizes.**

## What I rebuilt ([app.js](js/app.js), [style.css](css/style.css))

**Products → Add/Edit form** now has 11 fields instead of 6:

- **Main Category** — a Men / Women / Children / Other dropdown.
- **Sub-Category** — cascades from the main category: choosing Women lists only the 8 women's lines, Children lists Children's Fashion, Other lists Caps & Gift Cards. Selecting a main group auto-selects the right sub-category when editing.
- **Colours** — 10 clickable swatch toggles (was hard-coded to `black, navy, white`). Whatever you select becomes the colour dots shoppers see.
- **Sizes** — 8 size chips (XS–XXL, Free Size); when editing, the product's existing sizes are added to the pool so unusual ones (shoe sizes, kids' year bands) stay editable instead of being wiped.
- **Tags** — `new` / `featured` / `bestseller` / `sale` / `trending` chips. Previously every new product was forced to `['new']`; now the admin decides whether it feeds New Arrivals, Best Sellers or the sale carousel.
- **Description** — editable textarea (was a fixed sentence).
- Plus title, price, sale price (with a guard: sale price must be below regular price), stock, image URL.

**Categories tab** also changed: it now shows **Main Category | Sub-Category | Slug ID | Products** with a legend explaining the two levels, so you can see at a glance which group each sub-category sits under.

## Verified by doing it

Signed in as **NoFrame Admin** → dashboard opened (Overview, Products, Categories, Orders, Customers) → added a product as *Women → Women's Elegant Blouses* with colours white/beige/rose, sizes XS/M/L/XL/2XL, tags new+featured → it appeared in the category listing (3 colour dots) and on its product page with **Rs. 4,200 / Rs. 5,000 / SAVE 16%**, the right swatches, sizes and description. Then I opened it in **Edit** mode: every field pre-filled, deselected black/navy/S/`new`, saved, and the stored product came back with `mainCategory: "Women"` and the reduced lists. Test product deleted afterwards — back to 174.

Two bugs found and fixed during testing: `mainCategory` was saving as an empty string (wrong value type passed to the formatter), and a failed save logged a red *"Database save failed"* even though the browser copy had been written — it now warns accurately: `API unavailable (API 501) — product data is kept in this browser only. Start XAMPP/MySQL to persist it centrally.`

Assets bumped to `?v=20261031`; console is clean apart from the known static-server warnings and the by-design hero-video 404s.

**One caveat:** under the static preview, saves can only reach this browser (no PHP on port 8080). Under XAMPP with MySQL running, the same form writes to the database through `?action=save`, which accepts this admin's session and rejects everyone else with 403.
