The Returns view is built and verified in the browser.

## What was added

**Admin → Returns (`#/admin/returns`)** — [js/app.js](js/app.js), [css/style.css](css/style.css)

- New **Returns** item in the admin sidebar (between Orders and Customers) with a live counter: **Returns (1)** while a request is waiting on you — same pattern as the Questions counter.
- Stat strip across the top: **Return Requests · Awaiting Decision · Approved / Refunded · Value In Returns**.
- One row per return request, newest first, containing: product photo, item name (plus "how many more items" when the order had several), order id and order date, the **reason and note** with raised / decided / refunded timestamps, the **order amount**, a colour-coded status chip, and the actions.
- Status chips: **Requested** (amber), **Approved** (green), **Refunded** (violet), **Declined** (red), with the order's own status shown underneath.
- Actions on each row:
  - `Approve` / `Decline` while the request is **Requested**
  - `Mark as refunded` once it is **Approved**
  - closed (no buttons) once declined or refunded
  - a **View order** link that jumps to that order already expanded in the Orders tab
- Empty state explains that requests arrive from My Orders in a customer's profile.

**Shared decision logic** — `decideReturn()` in [js/app.js](js/app.js) now handles approve, decline and refund, and re-renders whichever screen you acted from (the Returns tab or the inline panel inside the order detail). Approving sets the order to **Returned**; refunding sets it to **Refunded** and stamps `refundedAt`. A refund is blocked until the return is approved — it shows "Approve the return before recording a refund" and changes nothing. `Refunded` was also added to the admin order status dropdown. The customer sees the same status back in their own order history.

## Verified in the browser

- Sidebar counter, two rows, all chip styles, stat strip and topbar ("1 awaiting decision") render correctly.
- Full lifecycle ran end to end: **Requested → Approve** (chip flips, order becomes `Returned`, buttons swap to *Mark as refunded*) **→ Refund** (`Refunded` chip, order `Refunded`, `refundedAt` written, confirmation toast).
- Guard tested: refunding a still-`Requested` return is refused and leaves the state untouched.
- The Orders tab still shows its inline return panel, and the status dropdown lists `Confirmed … Delivered, Returned, Refunded` with the row's current status selected.
- Console shows **no JavaScript errors** — only the pre-existing MySQL 500s.

Demo state left on screen: `NF900001` is **Requested** (so Approve/Decline are visible) and `NF900002` is **Approved** (so *Mark as refunded* is visible). Asset versions are bumped to `?v=20261031c` and the preview server is still running at 127.0.0.1:8090.

The one outstanding blocker is unchanged: the PHP API returns 500 because `$DB_PASS` in [api/config.php](api/config.php) is empty — put your real XAMPP MySQL password there and return decisions (and everything else) will persist to MySQL instead of the browser copy.
